    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4455" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλοθεν</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from another place</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ἄλλος</span> one <i>from one
				place</i>, another <i>from another</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.75
			</span></i>, etc., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				86
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				518
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				92
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				595
			</span></i>, etc. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. εἰλήλουθε</span> he
			came <i>from abroad</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.318
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποθεν ἄλλοθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					7.52
				</span></i>
			 ; in
				Att.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ὁθενοῦν</span> or
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁποθενοῦν</span>
			<i>from</i> what <i>other place</i> soever, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				738c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Grg.</u>
				512a
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδαμόθεν ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phlb.</u>
					3c
				</span></i>
			a : c. gen. loci, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. τῶν Ἑλλήνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					707e
				</span></i>
			.</div>
